    "features": "<p>When people slip past security, evade the authorities, or escape the military, they become prey for bounty hunters. Bounty hunters are often kept on retainer by corporations, including some security providers, or operate on their own or as a part of a larger team. Depending on their level of ethics, many prefer to earn their pay by bringing in the target dead rather than alive. Sometimes, that’s simply easier. Likewise, most professional bounty hunters cannot be paid off; however, part-time and amateur hunters might be willing to accept payment in lieu of capture. Of course, the bounty hunter might accept the bribe and turn in their quarry for payment. These stats represent a professional bounty hunter as opposed to an opportunistic pirate or a soldier with a side job. Those with years of experience have a correspondingly higher threat level (see The More Threatening Adversary).</p><p><strong>Favored Stunts:</strong> Called Shot, Efficient Gunner, Skirmish</p><p><strong>Talents:</strong> Expertise - Tracking (Expert), Living on the Fringe (Expert), Scouting (Expert)</p><p><strong>Equipment:</strong> knife, pistol, stun gun, light body armor, hand terminal, survival gear</p><p><strong>Armor + Toughness:</strong> 4</p>",
    "statBlockView": true
  },
